].[Cl-]","Type":"IC50"}],"logp":[{"abbreviation_in_the_article":"Os","value":0.995,"value_relation":"=","type_authors":"logD","method":"shake-flask","aqueous_phase":"PBS","doi":"10.1021/jacs.6c04446","year":2026,"counterion":"[Cl-].[Cl-]","record_id":"MLDB-002885","detection":"UV-Vis","method_description":"The distribution coefficient (LogD) of the compound was determined using the shakeflask method. Water-saturated 1-octanol and octanol-saturated PBS were prepared by equilibrating 1-octanol and PBS at a volume ratio of 4:1 (v/v) with shaking for 24 h at room temperature. The compound was diluted to 20 μM using water-saturated 1-octanol, followed by the addition of an equal volume of octanol-saturated PBS. The mixture was shaken overnight at room temperature at 200 rpm to reach partition equilibrium and then centrifuged at 10 000 × g for 2 min. The resulting organic and aqueous phases were then separated with a syringe, and the absorbance of each phase was measured using a microplate reader"}]}